course: dictionary
lesson: 8449
title: The Archer in the sky
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Sagittarius is a group of stars in the night sky. Astronomers call a group like this a constellation. Long ago, people pictured it in the southern sky as an archer, half man and half horse, aiming a bow.
explain: You can see it from Britain, but it sits low in the sky in summer. «Scorpius, with red Antares, and Sagittarius, shaped like a teapot, lie low in the south in summer from Britain but much higher from the southern US and Australia.» So where you live changes how high it looks.
explain: The word Sagittarius has other meanings too. In astrology it is one of the twelve star signs, and people born in late November to late December «are a Sagittarius». Astronomers also use the name for «Sagittarius A*», a giant black hole at the centre of our galaxy, which lies in the direction of this constellation.
fact: Sagittarius is a constellation, a group of stars that people have named and pictured in the night sky.
fact: The constellation Sagittarius is often shown as an archer, half man and half horse.
fact: «Sagittarius A*» is the name for a giant black hole at the centre of our galaxy, about 4 million times the mass of the Sun.
fact: A black hole is a place where gravity is so strong that not even light can escape.
fact: Astrology gives people star signs, but scientists say star signs cannot predict anyone's personality or future.
exercise: «Scorpius, with red Antares, and Sagittarius, shaped like a teapot, lie low in the south in summer.» What kind of thing is Sagittarius here? | *A group of stars in the night sky | A kind of metal teapot | A type of black hole | A month of the year
exercise: Ella's cousin says, «I am a Sagittarius, born in December.» What does she mean? | She was born on the Sun | *She has the star sign Sagittarius, one of the twelve in astrology | She works at a planetarium | She is an archer who rides a horse
exercise: What does «Sagittarius A*» name? | The brightest star in the night sky | A teapot-shaped group of stars | A planet beyond Mars | *A giant black hole at the centre of our galaxy
test: Sagittarius is often pictured as an archer who is half what and half what? | *Half man and half horse | Half bird and half fish | Half dog and half bear | Half lion and half goat
test: Why do scientists say star signs cannot tell the future? | Because the stars are too far away to see | Because star signs only work in summer | *Because astronomy is science, and star signs cannot predict anyone's personality or future | Because a black hole moves the signs around
exam: Why does Sagittarius look different in the sky from Britain than from Australia? | Because it can only be seen in winter | Because it is a black hole that moves across the sky | *Because it lies low in the south from Britain but much higher from Australia | Because its teapot shape changes every year
